# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore for deepgis-xr web image
# =============================================================================
# Background: the previous build's `COPY . .` step took ~8 minutes and the
# image-export step hung. The cause was a build context dominated by ~15 GB of
# files that have no business inside the image:
#
#   sam_vit_*.pth (4 GB)   — SAM weights, served by services/sam-api on the
#                            remote host (192.168.0.232).
#   yolov8*.pt    (137 MB) — YOLO weights, served by the remote YOLO container.
#   db.sqlite3    (1.8 GB) — local dev DB. Production uses Postgres (see the
#                            DATABASE_URL env var); dev mounts ./db.sqlite3 via
#                            the bind in docker-compose.yml.
#   deepgis_results/ (6.4 GB) — generated SAM/YOLO artefacts, bind-mounted into
#                            the container at runtime.
#   cache/        (1.1 GB) — local model/inference cache, also bind-mounted.
#
# Note: staticfiles/ (1.9 GB, mostly 3D STL/glTF assets in staticfiles/models/)
# is intentionally NOT excluded — collectstatic is disabled and Django serves
# this directory directly via STATICFILES_DIRS (see settings.py). It is also
# overlaid by the `.:/app` bind mount in docker-compose.yml during dev, but
# the image-baked copy is required for deployments without that bind.
#
# Excluding the items below turns a 15+ GB context into roughly 2 GB and keeps
# the image free of ML model weights, in line with the architecture where
# YOLO/SAM/Mask-R-CNN inference all run as remote services on 192.168.0.232.
# =============================================================================

# --- AI/ML model weights (served remotely on 192.168.0.232) ------------------
# SAM checkpoints (sam_vit_b/l/h)
sam_vit_*.pth
# Ultralytics YOLOv8 weights
yolov8*.pt
yolov11*.pt
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.engine
# (the *.pt / *.pth wildcards are intentionally broad — we don't ship any
# torch checkpoints in the image; if a future legitimate need arises, allow
# specific files with `!path/to/file.pt` underneath.)

# --- Local dev databases / data stores ---------------------------------------
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-wal

# --- Bind-mounted runtime directories ----------------------------------------
# (NOT excluding staticfiles/ — it's the served source-of-truth for STATICFILES_DIRS;
#  see the header comment.)
deepgis_results/
cache/
media/
mbtiles/
logs/
tmp_remote_inspect/
tmp_*/

# --- Stale STATIC_ROOT (collectstatic is intentionally disabled) -------------
# settings.py sets STATIC_ROOT = BASE_DIR/static/ but the project deliberately
# does NOT run collectstatic — Django serves STATICFILES_DIRS directly. Any
# files under ./static/ are stale leftovers from a previous experiment and
# should never be baked into the image (13 GB on the dev host).
static/

# --- Large data files served by sibling containers, not by web --------------
# data/ holds the mbtile vector / raster sources served by the tileserver-gl
# container (see docker-compose.yml `tileserver-gl` service which bind-mounts
# ./data:/data:ro). The deepgis-xr web container never opens these files, so
# they don't belong in the web image.
data/
*.mbtiles

# GeoTIFF rasters that were dropped under deepgis_xr/static/tifs/ for ad-hoc
# previewing (~11 GB on the dev host). Not referenced by Django code; if a
# future feature needs them it should be served via tileserver-gl or a CDN.
deepgis_xr/static/tifs/
*.tif
*.tiff

# --- Python / virtualenv noise -----------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
venv/
.venv/
env/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Git & IDE metadata ------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Node / frontend tooling (built assets are committed; src tooling isn't) -
node_modules/
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log
.pnpm-debug.log

# --- Archives & generated artefacts ------------------------------------------
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
*.7z
*.dmg
*.iso
*.log

# --- Docs / dev-only assets we don't need in the image -----------------------
docs/_build/
*.bak
*.backup
*.orig
*.rej
Dockerfile.cpu-backup
